/api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101976","id":2622680930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cUu9i","user":{"login":"hustlerone","id":167621692,"node_id":"U_kgDOCf20PA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/167621692?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone","html_url":"https://github.com/hustlerone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hustlerone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-29T19:42:28Z","updated_at":"2025-01-29T19:42:28Z","body":"> > The issue is the ColorRects inside the BackBufferCopy (you have to manually set their size and position yourself), not the Control itself.\n> \n> `ColorRect`s are controls, while `BackBufferCopy` is a `Node2D.` The same problem happens whenever you have a `Control` that is a child of a `Node2D`.\n> \n> The solution is to not have organize your `Control`s as children nodes of a `Node2D`\n\nThat is nice and all, but how am I supposed to do post processing effects then?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2622680930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2622779108","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101976#issuecomment-2622779108","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101976","id":2622779108,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6cVG7k","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-29T20:31:04Z","updated_at":"2025-01-29T20:31:04Z","body":"> > > The issue is the ColorRects inside the BackBufferCopy (you have to manually set their size and position yourself), not the Control itself.\n> > \n> > \n> > `ColorRect`s are controls, while `BackBufferCopy` is a `Node2D.` The same problem happens whenever you have a `Control` that is a child of a `Node2D`.\n> > The solution is to not have organize your `Control`s as children nodes of a `Node2D`\n> \n> That is nice and all, but how am I supposed to do post processing effects then?\n\nYou can follow along with the approach from the documentation https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/shaders/custom_postprocessing.html","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2622779108/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2913685048","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101976#issuecomment-2913685048","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101976","id":2913685048,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tq044","user":{"login":"bfloch","id":2116566,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMTY1NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2116566?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch","html_url":"https://github.com/bfloch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bfloch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T19:12:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T19:12:07Z","body":"The quoted documentation shows a control as shader owner and even mentions:\n\n> Another more efficient method is to use a [BackBufferCopy](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_backbuffercopy.html#class-backbuffercopy) to copy a region of the screen to a buffer and to access it in a shader script through a sampler2D using hint_screen_texture.\n\nAs the original poster reports the post processing positions do not propagate correctly.\n\nI found a similar issue in 4.2.2 where I had to set my mode from Rect to Viewport.\n4.2.1 works so I think the regression happened there.\n\nIt is still broken in 4.4.1.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2913685048/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534191301","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101976#issuecomment-3534191301","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101976","id":3534191301,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Sp3rF","user":{"login":"ghostsoft","id":63552156,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTUyMTU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63552156?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft","html_url":"https://github.com/ghostsoft","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghostsoft/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-14T19:11:32Z","updated_at":"2025-11-14T19:11:32Z","body":"I am also confused about this - why _is_ BackBufferCopy a Node2D anyway? The docs on postprocessing specifically mentions using BackBufferCopy and there's this line in the documentation for BackBufferCopy:\n\n> Note: Since this node inherits from [Node2D](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_node2d.html#class-node2d) (and not [Control](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_control.html#class-control)), anchors and margins won't apply to child [Control](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_control.html#class-control)-derived nodes. This can be problematic when resizing the window. To avoid this, add [Control](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_control.html#class-control)-derived nodes as siblings to the BackBufferCopy node instead of adding them as children.\n\nbut as far as I can tell if you add a Control node such as a ColorRect used for postprocessing as a sibling it will not actually benefit from the backbuffer and it needs to be a child of the node, thus bringing us back to the issue that it will no longer scale with the viewport (instead anchoring to whatever rect the BackBufferCopy has). It's incredibly unclear how this is supposed to be used for post-processing.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3534191301/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]